1
00:00:14,797 --> 00:00:17,367
This is my new home.

2
00:00:19,107 --> 00:00:20,277
Father,

3
00:00:20,757 --> 00:00:23,517
why am I here?

4
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:27,777
Why did Mother and Father not come for me?

5
00:00:28,137 --> 00:00:30,997
Is it because I am their bastard child?

6
00:00:37,827 --> 00:00:39,937
I don't need friends.

7
00:00:39,937 --> 00:00:41,887
I don't need companions.

8
00:00:41,887 --> 00:00:43,707
I don't need Father or Mother.

9
00:00:44,557 --> 00:00:46,707
I will become great.

10
00:00:47,137 --> 00:00:49,267
I will.

11
00:00:49,267 --> 00:00:52,917
I'll become great and look down on all of them.

12
00:00:57,227 --> 00:00:58,307
...Chief!

13
00:00:59,787 --> 00:01:01,257
Section Chief!

14
00:01:03,017 --> 00:01:05,477
Please wake up, Section Chief.

15
00:01:05,477 --> 00:01:08,497
Section Chief Maxwell.

16
00:01:11,487 --> 00:01:17,607
Anderson's armed priest squad that was sent earlier has secured Integra Hellsing,

17
00:01:17,607 --> 00:01:21,837
and is currently engaging the remnants of the Letztes Batallion.

18
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:24,297
Impetuous hothead.

19
00:01:24,297 --> 00:01:26,997
I specifically told them to avoid hostilities and to observe.

20
00:01:43,227 --> 00:01:45,527
That's quite a fire...

21
00:01:47,327 --> 00:01:49,317
Just like purgatory.

22
00:01:49,317 --> 00:01:51,737
The Imperial Capital, London, is completely devastated.

23
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:55,447
Not since the Great London Air Raid has there been such a fire.

24
00:01:55,447 --> 00:01:58,137
As for the current death toll, we cannot provide an estimate.

25
00:01:58,137 --> 00:02:02,237
In addition, we don't know how many of those have become undead.

26
00:02:02,967 --> 00:02:05,007
It's divine punishment.

27
00:02:05,007 --> 00:02:09,247
The fools stretched themselves into rapture and ignorantly embraced heresy.

28
00:02:09,667 --> 00:02:11,757
They got what they deserved.

29
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:13,807
Good riddance.

30
00:02:20,187 --> 00:02:21,597
And the United States?

31
00:02:21,597 --> 00:02:23,267
Major chaos.

32
00:02:23,267 --> 00:02:26,257
The White House is still in flames.

33
00:02:26,817 --> 00:02:31,897
It seems that a presidential aide turned into a vampire during a meeting.

34
00:02:32,207 --> 00:02:36,397
The president and all thirteen cabinet members were killed.

35
00:02:36,827 --> 00:02:39,027
Naturally, that would be the outcome.

36
00:02:39,027 --> 00:02:42,067
They're positioning themselves around the presidential residence.

37
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:45,527
If the damage escalates, have them take action.

38
00:02:45,927 --> 00:02:48,537
Otherwise, do not move a finger.

39
00:02:48,537 --> 00:02:51,907
Their chaos is beneficial for us.

40
00:02:51,907 --> 00:02:54,547
We'll maintain it as long as possible.

41
00:02:57,597 --> 00:03:03,157
But I don't understand why the Millennium hasn't advanced further.

42
00:03:03,157 --> 00:03:05,057
I couldn't care less.

43
00:03:05,057 --> 00:03:08,127
It's fine as long as we're not hindered by it.

44
00:03:08,127 --> 00:03:12,107
The only things I'm interested in are England, Hellsing and Alucard.

45
00:03:12,107 --> 00:03:13,637
And that pig...

46
00:03:13,637 --> 00:03:17,567
Even the Vatican doesn't see that fat major as an obstacle.

47
00:03:20,987 --> 00:03:22,787
I won't allow for it!

48
00:03:22,787 --> 00:03:26,117
We'll hit them from the flank with everything we've got!

49
00:03:26,117 --> 00:03:28,047
That's right, Brethren.

50
00:03:28,047 --> 00:03:34,127
We shall liberate Britain from the heretics and monsters!

51
00:03:36,577 --> 00:03:39,547
Heretics and monsters can all die.

52
00:03:39,547 --> 00:03:42,387
That's what I learned from Father!

53
00:03:44,087 --> 00:03:47,157
The Knights of the Courtland, Brethren of the Sword!

54
00:03:47,157 --> 00:03:49,917
All 340 members assembled.

55
00:03:50,717 --> 00:03:53,177
The Knights of the Order of Calatrava La Nueva.

56
00:03:53,177 --> 00:03:55,897
All 118 members assembled.

57
00:03:56,617 --> 00:03:59,557
The Knights of the Sacred Military Order of Saint Stephen of Tuscany.

58
00:03:59,557 --> 00:04:02,527
All 257 members assembled.

59
00:04:03,247 --> 00:04:04,697
The Knights of the Order of Malta.

60
00:04:04,697 --> 00:04:08,037
All 2457 members assembled.

61
00:04:35,517 --> 00:04:39,877
At the command of his Holiness the Pope, we have gathered together here.

62
00:04:39,877 --> 00:04:42,777
Along with our assemblage comes your promotion, Bishop Maxwell.

63
00:04:42,777 --> 00:04:45,207
You'll now be dubbed Archbishop Maxwell.

64
00:04:46,047 --> 00:04:49,937
Together, our army has formed the Ninth Crusade,

65
00:04:49,937 --> 00:04:55,077
which we entrust ultimate command to your grace, Archbishop Maxwell.

66
00:05:07,377 --> 00:05:09,247
Amen!

67
00:05:09,247 --> 00:05:11,807
I graciously accept this with all my body and soul.

68
00:05:11,807 --> 00:05:13,807
Your target is the British Empire:

69
00:05:13,807 --> 00:05:15,807
the dead city of London!

70
00:05:16,277 --> 00:05:18,627
Commence our reconquest!

71
00:05:18,627 --> 00:05:21,737
Reconquistadors, move out!

72
00:05:24,807 --> 00:05:42,257
Amen!

73
00:05:51,717 --> 00:05:54,587
Am I, a member of Section XIII,

74
00:05:54,587 --> 00:06:00,477
the one who was loathed and called a devil child, now an Archbishop...

75
00:06:00,477 --> 00:06:03,027
and leader of the Ninth Crusade?!

76
00:06:07,627 --> 00:06:08,977
Section Chief!

77
00:06:11,157 --> 00:06:12,747
What is it?

78
00:06:13,107 --> 00:06:14,357
L-Look at these!

79
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,957
Our satellite over the Atlantic Ocean just took these.

80
00:06:20,847 --> 00:06:22,757
It's moving...

81
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,837
It's moving this way!

82
00:06:24,837 --> 00:06:25,977
That's not possible...!

83
00:06:26,857 --> 00:06:28,277
To the conflagration?!

84
00:06:28,277 --> 00:06:28,967
How could it be sailing?!

85
00:06:29,367 --> 00:06:33,897
Its speed is only several knots, but it's definitely moving...

86
00:06:33,897 --> 00:06:34,977
towards London!

87
00:06:36,407 --> 00:06:38,027
Alucard...

88
00:06:38,027 --> 00:06:39,477
...is coming.

89
00:06:43,077 --> 00:06:44,307
I care not.

90
00:06:44,307 --> 00:06:49,017
Hellsing, the Millenium and Alucard will all cease to exist soon.

91
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:53,127
Ultimately, we will be the ones to rise victorious at the Ring.

92
00:06:53,127 --> 00:06:54,997
All forces, move out!

93
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:59,177
The time has come for us, earthly agents of God, to implement our mission on behalf of his wrath!

94
00:07:31,197 --> 00:07:35,197
Everyone is laughing as they willfully turn towards hell for their assault.

95
00:07:36,177 --> 00:07:40,957
Who in the world among that killing field will be left alive at the end?

96
00:07:40,957 --> 00:07:46,667
I'm sure every last one will end up dying as they laugh within the twilight.

97
00:08:37,127 --> 00:08:38,937
So nostalgic.

98
00:08:38,937 --> 00:08:40,957
I can smell everything.

99
00:08:48,957 --> 00:08:52,097
The scent of impaled men.

100
00:08:52,097 --> 00:08:55,257
The scent of dismembered women.

101
00:08:55,257 --> 00:08:58,357
The scent of burnt infants.

102
00:08:58,357 --> 00:09:02,037
The scent of the elderly shot to death.

103
00:09:03,767 --> 00:09:05,667
The scent of death.

104
00:09:05,667 --> 00:09:07,657
The scent of war!

105
00:09:09,267 --> 00:09:12,297
Here I come, Major.

106
00:09:16,057 --> 00:09:20,457
Zorin, you may proceed.

107
00:09:20,457 --> 00:09:21,807
Roger.

108
00:09:22,587 --> 00:09:24,717
Restart Zeppelin II engines!

109
00:09:24,717 --> 00:09:27,057
Zorin Blitz Task Force, move out!

110
00:09:31,567 --> 00:09:34,717
Your target is... Hellsing HQ!

111
00:09:55,827 --> 00:09:58,047
How many of us are left?

112
00:09:58,047 --> 00:10:00,237
Roughly half.

113
00:10:00,237 --> 00:10:02,577
They're stronger than we thought.

114
00:10:03,507 --> 00:10:04,567
Use the Thermit!

115
00:10:05,197 --> 00:10:07,347
Incinerate the Nazi corpses!

116
00:10:07,347 --> 00:10:09,537
Leave no remnants!

117
00:10:12,387 --> 00:10:14,687
I'll take my leave.

118
00:10:15,757 --> 00:10:17,157
Where do you think you're going?

119
00:10:17,777 --> 00:10:20,417
I'm returning to my manor.

120
00:10:20,417 --> 00:10:22,917
My duties await me there.

121
00:10:22,917 --> 00:10:25,877
Duties as a commander.

122
00:10:25,877 --> 00:10:28,167
That's why I must return.

123
00:10:28,167 --> 00:10:29,717
I don't think so.

124
00:10:29,717 --> 00:10:32,307
You're in our custody now.

125
00:10:34,887 --> 00:10:35,917
A light.

126
00:10:38,107 --> 00:10:40,637
May I get a light for my cigar?

127
00:10:42,927 --> 00:10:44,507
You brainless worm.

128
00:10:48,777 --> 00:10:49,767
A light.

129
00:10:53,537 --> 00:10:54,767
A light.

130
00:10:54,767 --> 00:10:57,147
Well... you do...

131
00:10:57,147 --> 00:11:00,587
realize the position you're in... right?

132
00:11:02,077 --> 00:11:02,987
Light.

133
00:11:20,877 --> 00:11:22,917
The threat of guns do not affect me.

134
00:11:22,917 --> 00:11:26,517
I'm going back to the manor, so shoot me or move.

135
00:11:31,017 --> 00:11:32,517
Stand down, Yumie.

136
00:11:33,897 --> 00:11:36,537
I-I'm not very good with this type of person...

137
00:11:36,537 --> 00:11:37,877
What do we do?

138
00:11:37,877 --> 00:11:42,087
W-We could tie her up a-and take her with us.

139
00:11:42,087 --> 00:11:43,187
A joke?!

140
00:11:43,187 --> 00:11:45,027
I can hear you!

141
00:11:48,017 --> 00:11:50,637
Is that acceptable, Section XIII?

142
00:11:51,327 --> 00:11:54,377
Is that acceptable, Anderson?

143
00:11:54,377 --> 00:11:55,937
'Course not.

144
00:11:55,937 --> 00:12:00,477
Forcing our will as a group on a single unarmed woman...

145
00:12:00,487 --> 00:12:03,367
We'd be just like rapists.

146
00:12:04,797 --> 00:12:06,707
Then I shall leave.

147
00:12:06,707 --> 00:12:09,187
But it's dangerous for a woman to walk alone at night.

148
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:10,387
Escort me.

149
00:12:10,387 --> 00:12:11,947
Understood.

150
00:12:11,947 --> 00:12:14,017
We will.

151
00:12:16,297 --> 00:12:18,357
I'm in a hurry, so let's go.

152
00:12:18,357 --> 00:12:20,357
Wait!

153
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:32,237
What the heck...

154
00:12:32,237 --> 00:12:34,397
This has gotten really bad...

155
00:12:34,397 --> 00:12:35,997
W-W-What should we do?

156
00:12:35,997 --> 00:12:38,377
The Section Chief is going to get mad again...

157
00:12:38,377 --> 00:12:43,857
W-Well, we're technically "securing" her, so he might not get mad...

158
00:12:43,857 --> 00:12:45,957
T-That's just twisting your words...

159
00:12:45,957 --> 00:12:47,637
Shut up!

160
00:12:48,837 --> 00:12:51,847
Heinkel, find us a ride.

161
00:12:51,847 --> 00:12:54,627
We're sitting ducks like this.

162
00:12:54,627 --> 00:12:55,557
Yes, sir...

163
00:12:56,177 --> 00:12:59,097
Is this all right, Father Anderson?

164
00:12:59,097 --> 00:13:02,067
It might be seen as a breach of authority.

165
00:13:02,067 --> 00:13:05,347
So be it, 'tis better this way.

166
00:13:05,347 --> 00:13:09,067
Maxwell's methods are too arrogant.

167
00:13:14,577 --> 00:13:17,077
We'll be reaching Hellsing HQ momentarily.

168
00:13:17,447 --> 00:13:18,447
All right.

169
00:13:18,447 --> 00:13:20,587
All personnel, prepare for combat.

170
00:13:21,307 --> 00:13:23,657
Support fire from the flagship has commenced.

171
00:13:23,667 --> 00:13:25,297
They're using V-1s.

172
00:13:27,627 --> 00:13:31,667
The Heralds of Deus Ex Machina, eh?

173
00:13:31,667 --> 00:13:34,157
Give Hellsing everything we've got!

174
00:13:42,687 --> 00:13:43,727
What the hell...?

175
00:13:47,297 --> 00:13:48,737
What...?

176
00:13:51,897 --> 00:13:54,027
What's happening to them?!

177
00:13:54,027 --> 00:13:56,037
They're being intercepted!

178
00:13:56,437 --> 00:13:58,987
The shots are coming from Hellsing HQ!

179
00:13:59,727 --> 00:14:01,127
Bastards!

180
00:14:06,297 --> 00:14:09,507
All the V-1s have been shot down!

181
00:14:09,507 --> 00:14:11,027
That's impossible.

182
00:14:11,027 --> 00:14:14,387
All twenty-four of them were taken down simultaneously...

183
00:14:16,387 --> 00:14:17,607
Searchlights!

184
00:14:17,607 --> 00:14:19,387
Shine them on Hellsing HQ!

185
00:14:19,387 --> 00:14:21,207
Please don't!

186
00:14:21,207 --> 00:14:22,607
Then we'll be the ones shot at!

187
00:14:23,057 --> 00:14:24,117
It makes no difference!

188
00:14:24,117 --> 00:14:26,607
That woman can already see us!

189
00:14:58,267 --> 00:15:01,137
Keep shooting, Miss.

190
00:15:03,087 --> 00:15:06,397
Those new weapons seem to be holding up nicely, Miss.

191
00:15:08,527 --> 00:15:12,527
Harkonnen II: 30mm semi-automatic cannon.

192
00:15:12,527 --> 00:15:15,537
It has a maximum range of 4000m,

193
00:15:15,537 --> 00:15:18,547
and weighs 345kg in total.

194
00:15:19,257 --> 00:15:23,617
It's even more ridiculous with you wielding it, Miss.

195
00:15:23,617 --> 00:15:27,777
Mr. Bernadotte, could you please stop calling me "Miss"?

196
00:15:28,557 --> 00:15:30,487
My name is Seras.

197
00:15:31,477 --> 00:15:34,097
My apologies, Miss!

198
00:15:37,027 --> 00:15:37,887
Hey...

199
00:15:39,267 --> 00:15:41,757
Can you see London, Miss?

200
00:15:43,707 --> 00:15:45,167
I can.

201
00:15:49,637 --> 00:15:54,507
Picadilly, Soho and the Covent Garden were all reduced to ashes.

202
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:57,617
That London now...

203
00:15:57,617 --> 00:16:00,387
has become a synonym for hell.

204
00:16:01,747 --> 00:16:04,437
I've never liked London.

205
00:16:04,437 --> 00:16:07,167
I found it too old-fashioned.

206
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:10,127
It didn't suit me one bit.

207
00:16:11,197 --> 00:16:17,137
But the cabaret our gang went to on the weekends served good beer.

208
00:16:17,587 --> 00:16:21,717
That old bartender would act like a fool and always gossiped, but I liked him.

209
00:16:22,967 --> 00:16:27,227
The hookers at the Spring Lodge Hotel were all stingy and ugly.

210
00:16:27,977 --> 00:16:28,977
But still,

211
00:16:28,977 --> 00:16:31,477
they always took good care of us.

212
00:16:31,477 --> 00:16:33,987
None of them deserve what's happening.

213
00:16:35,647 --> 00:16:41,577
That old barmaid at the cafe on Barnaby Street would always bring me fish and chips I didn't order.

214
00:16:42,147 --> 00:16:48,337
"Because I was a foreigner", she thought I should try the English specialty.

215
00:16:49,077 --> 00:16:52,797
And each time I told her I couldn't eat it because it was too greasy.

216
00:16:52,817 --> 00:16:57,177
But I couldn't say no to her, so I ate it anyway.

217
00:17:00,627 --> 00:17:03,917
I don't like London.

218
00:17:03,927 --> 00:17:10,707
But the bartender, the hookers and the lady at the cafe had nothing to do with this battle.

219
00:17:11,487 --> 00:17:14,567
This war and the vampires were irrelevant to them.

220
00:17:15,017 --> 00:17:16,567
That bastard Major,

221
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:18,567
Section XIII,

222
00:17:18,567 --> 00:17:20,317
the Letzte Battalion,

223
00:17:20,317 --> 00:17:23,817
and even us at Hellsing, mean nothing to them.

224
00:17:23,827 --> 00:17:29,527
But now they're all dead, feasting upon the other dead.

225
00:17:29,527 --> 00:17:32,607
I just can't stand it.

226
00:17:33,707 --> 00:17:36,837
Seras, let's get our revenge.

227
00:17:39,337 --> 00:17:41,387
Let's beat them.

228
00:17:41,387 --> 00:17:44,097
Let's beat the shit out of them.

229
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,837
I understand.

230
00:17:46,837 --> 00:17:49,257
I understand, Captain.

231
00:17:49,257 --> 00:17:50,847
I understand...

232
00:18:01,157 --> 00:18:04,247
Target the enemy's flying dreadnought!

233
00:18:04,247 --> 00:18:05,867
Prepare to fire cannons!

234
00:18:10,497 --> 00:18:11,787
Fire!

235
00:18:25,137 --> 00:18:26,727
Taking fire!

236
00:18:28,127 --> 00:18:29,997
Light them up!

237
00:18:30,637 --> 00:18:32,237
Light those...

238
00:18:32,927 --> 00:18:34,527
bastards up!

239
00:18:47,397 --> 00:18:49,877
Blocks 1, 3 and 4 were hit!

240
00:18:52,577 --> 00:18:55,077
There's been an explosion in Prep Room 2!

241
00:19:01,977 --> 00:19:04,477
Stern engines 4 and 5 have ceased functioning!

242
00:19:18,477 --> 00:19:21,507
We've lost 32% of our flight ability!

243
00:19:21,507 --> 00:19:22,127
First Lieutenant!

244
00:19:22,927 --> 00:19:23,757
We have to...

245
00:19:23,757 --> 00:19:25,487
We have to retreat!

246
00:19:25,487 --> 00:19:26,987
It's too late!

247
00:19:34,537 --> 00:19:39,337
This lightly armed ship is like a paper balloon against that kind of firepower.

248
00:19:39,337 --> 00:19:41,627
And it's too huge to evade.

249
00:19:42,247 --> 00:19:43,707
Descend!

250
00:19:43,707 --> 00:19:44,797
Take it down!

251
00:19:44,997 --> 00:19:46,637
We'll force land on them!

252
00:19:46,637 --> 00:19:49,107
Land on Hellsing HQ, no...

253
00:19:49,107 --> 00:19:51,347
on that bitch as well!

254
00:19:54,347 --> 00:19:56,517
On Seras Victoria!

255
00:20:17,747 --> 00:20:18,577
Go!

256
00:20:18,577 --> 00:20:19,827
Get out of there, Seras!

257
00:20:31,237 --> 00:20:35,677
Explosive incendiary grenades for wide-area field dominance...

258
00:20:35,677 --> 00:20:37,827
Vladimir...?

259
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,997
We've lost control!

260
00:21:03,997 --> 00:21:06,507
W-We're going to crash!

261
00:21:43,487 --> 00:21:44,157
They did it!

262
00:21:44,157 --> 00:21:45,137
They really did it!

263
00:21:49,137 --> 00:21:50,127
It's not over!

264
00:21:50,127 --> 00:21:51,227
That's right.

265
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:52,737
Not yet, Ladies.

266
00:21:52,737 --> 00:21:53,647
Open your eyes!

267
00:21:54,397 --> 00:21:55,637
Here they come.

268
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:03,147
They escaped just before impact!

269
00:22:03,147 --> 00:22:04,257
That's impossible!

270
00:22:04,257 --> 00:22:06,147
With no suspension?!

271
00:22:06,147 --> 00:22:07,617
That's right.

272
00:22:07,617 --> 00:22:09,827
They aren't human.

273
00:22:09,827 --> 00:22:11,397
They're monsters.

274
00:22:20,717 --> 00:22:22,287
Captain.

275
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:26,037
Get down here and re-equip, Miss.

276
00:22:26,037 --> 00:22:28,067
Yes, sir!

277
00:22:36,147 --> 00:22:38,097
Watch closely, Miss.

278
00:22:38,097 --> 00:22:40,617
We'll show you how Geese fight.

279
00:22:43,947 --> 00:22:46,157
It's our turn now.

280
00:22:46,677 --> 00:22:48,397
Here they come, guys.

281
00:22:49,367 --> 00:22:51,237
Time to work.

282
00:22:51,237 --> 00:22:52,647
Rock and roll!

283
00:22:54,957 --> 00:22:57,657
Forty-two survived the crash, sir!

284
00:22:57,657 --> 00:23:00,657
Those missiles took a large toll on us.

285
00:23:01,127 --> 00:23:06,167
More than half of our troops are gone, along with all of our heavy artillery.

286
00:23:06,567 --> 00:23:08,997
But we're all burning with valor and ready to go!

287
00:23:08,997 --> 00:23:11,997
What are our orders, First Lieutenent Zorin Blitz?

288
00:23:12,767 --> 00:23:14,307
We're fine.

289
00:23:14,307 --> 00:23:17,387
We have more than enough to massacre their pathetic squadron.

290
00:23:19,287 --> 00:23:20,887
Kill them...

291
00:23:24,017 --> 00:23:25,387
Kill them all!

292
00:23:29,767 --> 00:23:33,677
Miss, that's a prime example of a "vampire", don't you think?

293
00:23:34,297 --> 00:23:37,947
They have superhuman athletic abilities and reflexes.

294
00:23:37,947 --> 00:23:42,947
They thirst for blood like beasts and have a monstrous power.

295
00:23:42,947 --> 00:23:46,957
They can feel a human's killing intent, read his movements,

296
00:23:46,957 --> 00:23:49,957
feel the beat of his heart and move accordingly.

297
00:23:50,547 --> 00:23:52,957
They can easily dodge bullets and blades.

298
00:23:52,957 --> 00:23:56,467
They attack their opponent and take their blood, no?

299
00:23:56,467 --> 00:23:59,477
So... how 'bout we try this instead?

300
00:24:07,887 --> 00:24:08,877
Land mines!

301
00:24:08,877 --> 00:24:09,857
They're using land mines!

302
00:24:12,687 --> 00:24:14,277
They stopped.

303
00:24:14,277 --> 00:24:15,187
Do it.

304
00:24:36,337 --> 00:24:37,787
Bingo.

305
00:24:38,087 --> 00:24:40,757
That's what you get for taking humans so lightly.

306
00:24:41,527 --> 00:24:44,037
Y-You resorted to such trickery?

307
00:24:44,037 --> 00:24:45,607
Trickery?

308
00:24:45,607 --> 00:24:49,757
They're idiots for rushing at us head-on.

309
00:24:50,557 --> 00:24:53,907
Land mines have no killing intent, no heartbeat, certainly no movement,

310
00:24:53,917 --> 00:24:56,777
and a direct, unavoidable, general attack area.

311
00:24:57,497 --> 00:25:01,637
Tiny shrapnel ejected by 60 consecutively exploding claymore mines,

312
00:25:01,937 --> 00:25:04,487
if you think you can dodge that, go ahead.

313
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:08,467
You see, we're weak at fighting.

314
00:25:08,467 --> 00:25:12,287
Like we'll fight fair and square when it'd be so damn scary.

315
00:25:12,287 --> 00:25:14,247
Got it, Mr. Soldiers?

316
00:25:15,377 --> 00:25:16,277
3rd floor!

317
00:25:16,277 --> 00:25:17,397
Send a fusillade of grenades...

318
00:25:18,037 --> 00:25:19,877
Keep a wide field of fire!

319
00:25:19,877 --> 00:25:21,967
Don't give em' any breathing room!

320
00:25:25,657 --> 00:25:26,427
Area!

321
00:25:26,637 --> 00:25:28,917
Aim accurately at areas instead of one guy.

322
00:25:33,187 --> 00:25:37,937
Rifle squad, concentrate all your fire on the vicinity of your primary targets.

323
00:25:37,937 --> 00:25:39,937
Focus fire!

324
00:25:39,937 --> 00:25:41,437
Captain!

325
00:25:42,387 --> 00:25:44,827
They've halted their advance.

326
00:25:44,827 --> 00:25:48,817
They've taken cover behind a hillcock and aren't budging.

327
00:25:49,787 --> 00:25:52,037
The bastards are hatchin' a plot.

328
00:25:52,037 --> 00:25:53,947
We'll be fine for now.

329
00:25:53,977 --> 00:25:57,707
We'll win as long as they don't get close.

330
00:25:58,177 --> 00:26:02,827
This is our first time watching the manor, though it's for money.

331
00:26:02,827 --> 00:26:06,707
We're dead meat if we let those scary men inside.

332
00:26:07,757 --> 00:26:10,627
'Cause we're weak at close quarters.

333
00:26:20,647 --> 00:26:23,287
I wonder if they'll withdraw...

334
00:26:23,287 --> 00:26:24,817
If they were normal.

335
00:26:32,997 --> 00:26:37,677
They'd be long gone if they were typical humans.

336
00:26:38,647 --> 00:26:41,037
But those bastards aren't your average human.

337
00:26:43,057 --> 00:26:44,637
They're monsters.

338
00:27:15,247 --> 00:27:16,737
W-What the...?

339
00:27:37,047 --> 00:27:38,267
What is that?

340
00:27:38,757 --> 00:27:40,987
What the hell is that?!

341
00:27:52,117 --> 00:27:53,017
What is it?!

342
00:27:53,707 --> 00:27:55,267
H-Hey!

343
00:27:55,267 --> 00:27:57,117
Is this a nightmare?!

344
00:27:57,117 --> 00:27:58,417
What's wrong?!

345
00:27:58,417 --> 00:27:59,487
What's going on there?!

346
00:27:59,487 --> 00:28:00,817
Don't stop shooting!

347
00:28:00,817 --> 00:28:01,877
Hey!

348
00:28:03,807 --> 00:28:05,397
Why'd you guys stop?!

349
00:28:06,627 --> 00:28:08,007
Hey, what's wrong?!

350
00:28:12,607 --> 00:28:14,577
H-Hey...

351
00:28:14,577 --> 00:28:16,177
You've got to be shitting me...

352
00:28:16,177 --> 00:28:17,727
Hey!

353
00:28:42,787 --> 00:28:44,857
T-That's-

354
00:28:44,857 --> 00:28:47,207
What the fuck is this shit?!

355
00:29:09,637 --> 00:29:11,517
Help me!

356
00:29:10,437 --> 00:29:11,877
It's a monster!

357
00:29:11,517 --> 00:29:13,147
My leg! My leg!

358
00:29:14,037 --> 00:29:17,177
My... My... My arm...

359
00:29:18,577 --> 00:29:20,137
Help me...

360
00:29:20,137 --> 00:29:20,937
I can't move...

361
00:29:42,507 --> 00:29:44,237
No way...

362
00:29:44,237 --> 00:29:46,167
That's not real...

363
00:29:47,477 --> 00:29:53,367
I don't know why I can say that, but something inside tells me...

364
00:29:53,367 --> 00:29:55,547
it's not real.

365
00:29:59,987 --> 00:30:03,187
Another eye on the forehead.

366
00:30:03,187 --> 00:30:05,137
That's what I taught you, right?

367
00:30:05,137 --> 00:30:06,407
Your third eye.

368
00:30:11,627 --> 00:30:14,447
Abandon those human eyes of yours.

369
00:30:14,917 --> 00:30:16,837
If you were a human, it'd become a problem.

370
00:30:17,767 --> 00:30:21,137
But you're no longer human.

371
00:30:21,637 --> 00:30:24,017
...No longer human!

372
00:30:30,267 --> 00:30:32,207
Illusion...?

373
00:30:33,917 --> 00:30:35,507
It's an illusion!

374
00:30:37,077 --> 00:30:38,147
It's a monster!

375
00:30:38,147 --> 00:30:39,737
Help me!

376
00:30:39,737 --> 00:30:41,697
M-M-My arm...

377
00:30:41,697 --> 00:30:43,777
Sn-Snap out of it!

378
00:30:43,777 --> 00:30:44,607
It's not real!

379
00:30:45,177 --> 00:30:46,537
Help me...!

380
00:30:46,537 --> 00:30:48,137
I can't move...

381
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:50,687
It's just an illusion!

382
00:30:50,687 --> 00:30:52,127
Impossible!

383
00:30:52,127 --> 00:30:53,377
This can't be real...

384
00:30:53,727 --> 00:30:55,847
No fucking way.

385
00:30:55,847 --> 00:30:57,377
Captain, it's an illusion!

386
00:30:57,377 --> 00:30:59,127
An illusion!

387
00:30:59,897 --> 00:31:01,597
Captain!

388
00:31:53,787 --> 00:31:54,887
W-What was that?

389
00:31:55,887 --> 00:31:58,397
M-My arm... isn't gone!

390
00:31:58,767 --> 00:32:00,567
W-What?

391
00:32:00,567 --> 00:32:01,907
What was that?

392
00:32:02,487 --> 00:32:04,537
W-What just happened there?

393
00:32:04,907 --> 00:32:06,467
Snap out of it!

394
00:32:06,467 --> 00:32:09,777
It was just an illusion caused by illusion techniques!

395
00:32:10,497 --> 00:32:11,867
Illusion techniques?

396
00:32:11,867 --> 00:32:13,347
That was an illusion?!

397
00:32:13,347 --> 00:32:14,457
Really?!

398
00:32:14,457 --> 00:32:15,417
Yes!

399
00:32:15,417 --> 00:32:17,867
That's precisely what it was.

400
00:32:17,867 --> 00:32:21,327
Congratulations for seeing through it, Seras Victoria.

401
00:32:21,327 --> 00:32:22,497
But...

402
00:32:22,497 --> 00:32:24,347
But you're too late!

403
00:33:09,227 --> 00:33:10,577
This is bad.

404
00:33:10,577 --> 00:33:12,357
They broke our front lines.

405
00:33:13,097 --> 00:33:14,347
This is the forward squad.

406
00:33:14,347 --> 00:33:16,847
The enemies have arrived here!

407
00:33:16,847 --> 00:33:18,607
They're storming our position!

408
00:33:31,167 --> 00:33:33,247
Stop their advance.

409
00:33:33,247 --> 00:33:36,737
Spread out and retrieve the others out there.

410
00:33:36,747 --> 00:33:39,747
Gather the rest of our men back here.

411
00:33:39,747 --> 00:33:43,087
Carry whatever weapons and grenades you can find.

412
00:33:44,767 --> 00:33:45,747
Miss...

413
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:47,507
Y-Yes, sir?

414
00:33:48,327 --> 00:33:51,007
We're going to barricade ourselves in this section of the manor.

415
00:33:51,007 --> 00:33:52,517
We'll be on the defensive,

416
00:33:53,167 --> 00:33:55,267
and you'll be on the offensive.

417
00:33:56,027 --> 00:33:58,397
We'll protect this place,

418
00:33:58,397 --> 00:34:01,897
while you beat those Nazi bastards to a pulp.

419
00:34:01,897 --> 00:34:03,387
Y-Yes, sir!

420
00:34:04,187 --> 00:34:06,777
Miss, you're our trump card.

421
00:34:06,777 --> 00:34:07,777
Lay waste to them,

422
00:34:08,857 --> 00:34:12,787
before they overrun us.

423
00:34:15,907 --> 00:34:17,667
We're counting on you.

424
00:34:26,207 --> 00:34:28,207
Y-Yes!

425
00:34:28,207 --> 00:34:31,437
Oh, I forgot one last thing.

426
00:34:31,437 --> 00:34:32,427
Seras!

427
00:34:33,037 --> 00:34:33,927
Yes, sir?!

428
00:34:33,927 --> 00:34:35,597
Close your eyes!

429
00:34:45,237 --> 00:34:50,377
W-What are you doing?!

430
00:34:50,377 --> 00:34:51,707
No fair, Captain!

431
00:34:51,707 --> 00:34:53,247
No fair!

432
00:34:53,247 --> 00:34:55,737
All right, time to move out! Hurry!

433
00:34:55,737 --> 00:34:57,207
Don't change the subject!

434
00:34:57,207 --> 00:34:59,207
Damn, I wanted to do that!

435
00:34:59,207 --> 00:35:02,897
Me too...

436
00:35:02,897 --> 00:35:04,947
Idiots!

437
00:35:11,087 --> 00:35:12,967
Miss Seras.

438
00:35:15,607 --> 00:35:18,007
Be sure not to die.

439
00:35:18,007 --> 00:35:19,477
Come back alive.

440
00:35:22,917 --> 00:35:24,317
You too, Captain.

441
00:35:24,317 --> 00:35:25,477
And everyone also.

442
00:35:33,597 --> 00:35:34,587
All right...

443
00:35:34,587 --> 00:35:35,487
Go!

444
00:35:36,367 --> 00:35:37,537
Heading out!

445
00:35:43,817 --> 00:35:45,417
She's a sweet kid.

446
00:35:46,467 --> 00:35:47,337
Yeah...

447
00:35:47,727 --> 00:35:50,087
She's ridiculously sweet.

448
00:35:54,627 --> 00:35:58,597
Letting such a sweet girl die would kill any man's pride.

449
00:35:58,597 --> 00:36:01,307
We would go to hell, yeah.

450
00:36:02,307 --> 00:36:03,947
That's right.

451
00:36:04,977 --> 00:36:06,267
Couldn't be more right.

452
00:36:06,267 --> 00:36:08,037
Very true, very true.

453
00:36:09,277 --> 00:36:12,647
Sorry, but your lives will be thrown away.

454
00:36:13,467 --> 00:36:16,257
You shall be buried here.

455
00:36:16,257 --> 00:36:18,407
Your fortress will become your grave.

456
00:36:18,777 --> 00:36:21,717
Captain, you should say:

457
00:36:21,717 --> 00:36:25,827
"If the rest of you want to flee, then do it while you can."

458
00:36:25,827 --> 00:36:28,917
Or "Everyone run, I'll fight here alone."

459
00:36:28,917 --> 00:36:30,417
Something like that.

460
00:36:30,417 --> 00:36:32,907
What are you blabbering about?

461
00:36:32,907 --> 00:36:37,187
You guys are willing to fight a war for some small change.

462
00:36:37,717 --> 00:36:39,547
You disrespect your parents.

463
00:36:39,547 --> 00:36:40,617
That's true.

464
00:36:40,617 --> 00:36:42,677
He's right.

465
00:36:42,677 --> 00:36:44,447
That's right.

466
00:36:46,617 --> 00:36:48,707
Well then...

467
00:36:49,637 --> 00:36:51,807
Let's go and die, dogs.

468
00:36:51,807 --> 00:36:55,077
Let's go and die screaming "Fuck, fuck!"

469
00:36:55,077 --> 00:36:57,207
Take a shot in the gut

470
00:36:57,207 --> 00:36:59,197
and writhe on the ground.

471
00:37:00,797 --> 00:37:02,077
Sounds great to me!

472
00:37:02,077 --> 00:37:03,957
Can't agree with you more.

473
00:37:03,957 --> 00:37:07,087
You're absolutely right!

474
00:37:26,727 --> 00:37:28,737
It's only begun...

475
00:37:28,737 --> 00:37:32,227
The war has only just begun.

476
00:37:33,087 --> 00:37:34,317
More...

477
00:37:35,297 --> 00:37:38,317
Become even more magnificent!

478
00:37:40,577 --> 00:37:43,837
If you don't... I'll be deeply...

479
00:37:43,837 --> 00:37:45,637
troubled.

480
00:37:59,627 --> 00:38:02,377
You will not be forgiven...

481
00:38:02,377 --> 00:38:05,267
You will not be saved!

482
00:41:43,927 --> 00:41:49,287
Shoot!

483
00:41:50,947 --> 00:41:54,597
Bastards!

484
00:41:56,737 --> 00:42:00,997
Now... all of you just hurry up and die!

485
00:42:00,997 --> 00:42:02,787
Scum!

